    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306-a2">

                <pb facs="0435" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg355"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Squiers to Mr. Montes, acting secretary of state
                        and justice</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The first secretary of this
                    legation is in receipt of a communication from the judge of the first instance,
                    requesting him to appear at court to give testimony in a case of robbery which
                    recently occurred at the legation.</p>
                <p>While I have no objection to having the first secretary give testimony on terms
                    consistent with representative dignity, I must nevertheless inform your
                    excellency that unless interrogatory in open court is absolutely indispensable,
                    I much prefer personal deposition at the legation.</p>
                <p>Trusting that this course may meet with the approval of the Government of your
                    excellency, I improve the occasion, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
